# .agentignore — path and content policy for agent tooling.
#
# Scope: protects against curious agents stumbling into protected paths and
# high-confidence secret patterns leaking back to the model.
#
# Out of scope: adversarial exfil (compiled binaries, network calls,
# custom-format secrets), shell globs and runtime-built paths, base64 or other
# indirection, hardlinks and symlinks to protected files, and path-existence
# leaks via listings. See the README's four limits — each is a decision, not an
# oversight.
#
# PostToolUse: a matched `scrub:` pattern replaces the entire tool result
# with a placeholder before the model sees it. The hook does not attempt
# partial redaction; consider that cost before adding aggressive patterns.
#
# How to add:
#   - Path rules: gitignore-style lines (e.g. `private/`). Supported syntax:
#     leading `/` anchors to the repo root, trailing `/` marks a directory,
#     `*`, `**`, `?` are wildcards, `!` negates, `#` comments.
#   - Content patterns: `scrub: <regex>` lines, matched case-insensitively
#     against tool result text. Comment a line out to relax.
#   - The policy file, the hook, and harness settings are always blocked.

# Path patterns (gitignore-style)
secrets/api-key.txt
private/
.env

# Content patterns (PostToolUse block-on-match)
scrub: \bsk_(live|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}\b
scrub: \bgh[pous]_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}\b
scrub: \bAKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}\b
scrub: -----BEGIN (RSA |EC |OPENSSH |PGP )?PRIVATE KEY-----
scrub: \beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\b
